  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Triangle passing forwards and back",
  "description": "Three players and one ball. The players form a triangle with depth: one further back and two further forward at different heights – not all three in a row. The ball goes forwards and backwards in the triangle, not just sideways.\n\nA passes forward to B, B passes on forward to C, and C passes back to A. The receiver shows with the stick where they want the ball. After a while the players start moving: whoever has passed skates to a new spot so the triangle always keeps its depth.\n\nProgression: two touches, then one touch. Run several triangles on the ice at once. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Show with the stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stop the ball and look up before passing on."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep depth in the triangle – don't stand in line with the others."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Pass in front of your team-mate's stick so they can keep going forward."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
